{"attempt": 1, "baseline_version": null, "cached_tokens": 96607, "completed_at": "2026-09-28T14:34:01Z", "conversation_id": "d22b2015bc7c436c9e629188f47dff20", "cost_usd": 0.11427880000000003, "dataset": "dry-run", "diagnosis_elapsed_sec": 164.81211204174906, "diagnosis_family": null, "diagnosis_location": null, "diagnosis_text": "### Diagnosis\n\nThe slowdown localises to the **s1\u2013s5 inter-switch link**, particularly the **s1 port 4 \u2192 s5 port 1 direction**.\n\nEvidence:\n\n- h1\u2192h5 ping: **0% loss**, but very high **96 ms average RTT**.\n- h1\u2192h5 TCP: sender managed only **~0.35 Mbit/s**.\n- h1\u2192h2, local to s3: **~11 Gbit/s**, so h1 and its access port are healthy.\n- h2\u2192h3, traversing s3\u2013s1 and s1\u2013s4: **~6.72 Gbit/s**, clearing the s3\u2013s1 portion.\n- h2\u2192h5 and h2\u2192h6 were both extremely slow, implicating the path into s5 rather than h5 alone.\n- h5\u2192h6, switched locally on s5: **~10.36 Gbit/s**, clearing s5\u2019s host-facing ports and local switching.\n- h3\u2192h5, which also crosses s1\u2013s5, delivered only **~0.44 Mbit/s** with **73 retransmissions**.\n\nONOS reports the link as active and enabled. No port errors or drops were observed, and the idle link sample showed no queue backlog. Therefore, this looks more like **delay/rate limiting or another traffic-control impairment** on `s1:4`/`s5:1`, rather than a failed link or ordinary packet-error condition.\n\n**Next step:** inspect the queueing/traffic-control configuration on the interfaces corresponding to **s1 port 4 and s5 port 1**, starting with **s1\u2019s egress toward s5**. A reverse-direction throughput test would additionally establish whether the impairment is directional.", "dry_run_kind": "paired-pipeline", "elapsed_sec": 164.81211204174906, "error": null, "evaluation_error": null, "experiment_version": "protocol-v1", "failure_class": null, "family_correct": 1, "first_token_seconds": 159.80591077404097, "formal": false, "full_diagnosis_correct": 1, "git_commit": "b3d403846de77792fa912217490ce302cb17956a", "git_dirty": true, "ground_truth_family": "congestion", "include_in_accuracy": true, "input_tokens": 107286, "interleave_index": null, "invalid_tool_calls": 0, "label": "DRY RUN / NOT FORMAL DATA", "location_correct": 1, "method": "llm", "model": "gpt-5.6-sol", "model_calls": 15, "outcome": "scored", "output_tokens": 1646, "primary_conclusion_span": "ONOS reports the link as active and enabled. No port errors or drops were observed, and the idle link sample showed no queue backlog. Therefore, this looks more like **delay/rate limiting or another traffic-control impairment** on `s1:4`/`s5:1`, rather than a failed link or ordinary packet-error condition.", "prompt": "Transfers from h1 to h5 are very slow. Investigate and localise the cause.", "prompt_sha256": "9d8d23895207994407609a081e431633f78df07c9d29d40856055aaf2fdd4ad4", "random_seed": 6200, "reasoning_effort": "medium", "reasoning_tokens": 890, "repetition": null, "rescore_note": "Evaluator span fix applied to the stored dry-run text. The model was not called again.", "reset_verified": true, "reset_verified_after": true, "reset_verified_before": true, "run_id": "affbc2990e2543d7b612acb731b884a7", "run_order": null, "scenario": "F2", "scoring_version": "protocol-v1", "started_at": "2026-09-28T14:31:11Z", "tool_call_count": 14, "tool_calls": [{"arguments": {}, "elapsed_sec": 0.08586343191564083, "invalid": false, "ok": true, "sequence": 1, "tool": "get_topology"}, {"arguments": {"count": 5, "dst": "h5", "src": "h1"}, "elapsed_sec": 4.217159926425666, "invalid": false, "ok": true, "sequence": 2, "tool": "ping"}, {"arguments": {"dst": "h5", "duration": 3, "src": "h1"}, "elapsed_sec": 4.2092083264142275, "invalid": false, "ok": true, "sequence": 3, "tool": "iperf"}, {"arguments": {"sw": "s3"}, "elapsed_sec": 0.028528747148811817, "invalid": false, "ok": true, "sequence": 4, "tool": "get_flow_table"}, {"arguments": {"sw": "s1"}, "elapsed_sec": 0.0309898